<title>USA: Fed re-adds reserves via 14-day/overnight repos.</title>
<headline>Fed re-adds reserves via 14-day/overnight repos.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve added temporary reserves to the U.S. banking system on Thursday via overnight and 14-day fixed system repurchase agreements after earlier operations were cancelled due to technical problems, a Fed spokesman said.</p>
<p>At 1210 EDT/1610 GMT, federal funds were quoted at 5-1/4 percent, in line with the central bank's target for the rate.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1676</p>
</text>
